<p>When your business keeps its clients' details in Shadetree (names, contact details, addresses, photos, quotes and invoices), your business decides what to collect and why. Shadetree processes that data on your behalf, following your instructions. This page summarises how; it forms part of our <%= link_to "Terms of Service", terms_path %>.</p>

<h2>What we do with your clients' data</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Store it, show it to your team according to their roles, and include it in the quotes, invoices, emails and client pages you send.</li>
  <li>Send emails and messages to your clients only when you or your settings ask us to.</li>
  <li>Back it up, and keep it secure.</li>
</ul>
<p>We don't use your clients' data for anything else: no advertising, no selling, no contacting your clients ourselves.</p>

<h2>Our people</h2>
<p>Only a small number of Shadetree staff can reach your data, only to support you or keep the service running. Access through our support tools needs two-factor sign-in and is recorded in an audit log that can't be changed.</p>

<h2>Sub-processors</h2>
<p>We use the companies on our <%= link_to "Sub-processors", legal_document_path("subprocessors") %> page. We'll update that page before adding a new one.</p>

<h2>Requests from your clients</h2>
<p>If a client asks you for their data or to be forgotten, you can export it, or erase their details while keeping your financial records, from within Shadetree. If a client contacts us directly, we'll pass the request to you.</p>

<h2>Incidents</h2>
<p>If we learn of a breach affecting your clients' data, we'll tell you without undue delay, with what we know, so you can meet your own obligations.</p>

<h2>When you leave</h2>
<p>You can download all your data at any time. When your business is closed, its data is removed from Shadetree straight away; backups that still hold it expire within 12 months and are only used to restore the service.</p>
